    {
      "event": "teaching_chunk",
      "unit_id": "u2",
      "method": "worked_example",
      "content": "# How `await` Suspends and Resumes via the Generator Protocol\n\nPython's `async/await` syntax is sugar over generators. When you write `await something`, the coroutine **yields a Future** up to the event loop and is paused. The loop later calls `send(value)` on the coroutine to resume it. This example builds the chain by hand so you can see it.\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\n\nclass MyFuture:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self._value = value\n    def __await__(self):\n        yield self          # ← suspends; hands self up to the loop\n        return self._value  # ← runs after loop calls send(value)\n\nasync def inner():\n    print(\"[inner] awaiting Future\")\n    result = await MyFuture(42)\n    print(f\"[inner] resumed with {result}\")\n    return result * 2\n\nasync def outer():\n    print(\"[outer] calling inner()\")\n    return await inner()\n\nresult = asyncio.run(outer())\nprint(f\"final: {result}\")\n```\n\n## Step-by-step trace\n\n1. **`asyncio.run(outer())`** wraps `outer()` in a Task; loop calls `Task.__step` which calls `coro.send(None)`.\n2. **`outer` calls `inner()`** — delegation pushes execution into `inner`.\n3. **`inner` hits `await MyFuture(42)`** — `MyFuture.__await__` is invoked, yields `self`.\n4. **The yield bubbles all the way up** through `inner → outer → Task.__step`. The Task records the yielded Future and returns control.\n5. **Loop \"does I/O\"** — in a real loop this is where `select()` blocks. Here we instantly resolve `value_to_send = 42`.\n6. **`coro.send(42)`** re-enters the chain; `__await__` returns 42, `inner` computes `42 * 2 = 84`, `StopIteration(84)` propagates.\n7. **`outer` returns 84** — `Task` completes.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nEvery `await expr` compiles to `yield from expr.__await__()`. The loop only ever sees **one Future at a time** — the intermediate `yield from` links are transparent wiring. The classic gotcha is calling a CPU-bound function without `await` (or `run_in_executor`): no Future is ever yielded, `Task.__step` never returns, and the **entire event loop freezes**."
    },
